{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXEftuSY8K2XMe4eE8tq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the spec to `specs/feature-1-comment-editing.md`. It names each rule and its source without copying values. The answers and the source conflict are below, with values, since the spec leaves them out.\n\n**Answers to the six questions**\n\n1. **Who may edit:** only the comment author. The owner is the `authorId` field (`code-comment-ownership.md`). The soft-delete policy covers deletion, not editing, so I did not use it here.\n2. **Edit window:** 15 minutes after creation, per `policy-edit-window.md`. After that the API refuses the edit.\n3. **Edited mark:** a nullable `editedAt` timestamp, null until the first edit, set to the edit time on each successful edit. The migration that adds it must not change existing rows (`policy-edited-at-marker.md`). The current `Comment` model has no such field (`code-comment-model.md`).\n4. **Error shape and codes:** `policy-error-response.md` says new errors use `{\"errors\": {<field>: [messages]}}` with no wrapper. `code-error-shape.md` lists the codes in use today: 422 for validation, 401 for a missing or bad token, and 500 for other errors.\n5. **Migrations:** one timestamped folder per migration in `app/src/prisma/migrations`, applied with `npx prisma migrate deploy` using `DATABASE_URL` (`code-migrations.md`). `policy-release-checklist.md` adds two requirements: run that command against a fresh database, and give each migration a one-line undo note.\n6. **Unit tests:** `*.test.ts` files under `app/src/tests/services` and `app/src/tests/utils`, run with `npx nx test api`. The database is mocked, so no Postgres is needed (`code-test-layout.md`).\n\n**Conflict: error body shape**\n\n- `policy-error-response.md` says the errors-key shape, for example `{\"errors\":{\"body\":[\"can't be blank\"]}}`, with no extra wrapper.\n- `code-error-shape.md` gives that same shape for 422. It also gives a 401 body of `{\"status\":\"error\",\"message\":\"missing authorization credentials\"}` and a 500 body that is the bare error message.\n\nI followed the policy for new responses, because it is the rule for new work. The code file describes what exists today. Existing 401 and 500 responses do not match the policy, and I did not change them.\n\n**Gap: no status code for two refusals**\n\nNo source gives a status code for an edit refused because the window has passed, or because the caller is not the author. The only nearby rule is the delete path, which returns 404 for both cases. I did not invent a code. The Builder needs a decision before coding.\n\n**Other notes**\n\n- The auth header and JWT rules are included because they decide who the caller is. The header accepts only the Token or Bearer scheme.\n- The spec's plan has three steps: add the marker with its migration and undo note, add the edit path with ownership and window checks, and add unit tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3166,"cache_read_input_tokens":8124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3166,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ace4a105-fd83-4e3a-be14-acbaff22577c","uuid":"c0bb54ce-23ae-4ce8-98f4-3afac2ba2951","timestamp":"2026-10-29T21:27:04.637Z","request_id":"req_011CgXEftY89xR5TJLxhvANJ"}
